{
  "title": "M8 LPP Emulator",
  "children": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "lines": [
        "Launchpad Pro",
        "emulator for the",
        "Dirtywave M8.",
        "",
        "Maps Move's pads,",
        "buttons, and knobs",
        "to Launchpad Pro",
        "protocol for M8",
        "control.",
        "",
        "Requires M8 device",
        "connected via USB.",
        "",
        "M8 and the Launchpad",
        "talk on MIDI channels",
        "1-3. Keep Move",
        "tracks and Schwung",
        "slots on channel 4",
        "or higher, receive",
        "AND forward - a",
        "track listening on",
        "1-3 and sending to",
        "1-3 echoes M8 back",
        "at itself."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Controls",
      "children": [
        {
          "title": "Pads",
          "lines": [
            "8x4 pad grid maps",
            "to Launchpad Pro",
            "10x10 grid.",
            "",
            "The MODE BUTTON for",
            "the screen you are",
            "already on switches",
            "which half you see:",
            "Back on Session,",
            "Menu on Note,",
            "Capture on",
            "Sequencer.",
            "",
            "Pressing a different",
            "mode button changes",
            "screen instead. Each",
            "screen remembers the",
            "half YOU left it on,",
            "so going back to one",
            "puts you where you",
            "were, not on the top.",
            "",
            "Rows count from the",
            "TOP: row 1 is the",
            "top row, which is",
            "song row 00 on M8.",
            "",
            "Views: Top rows",
            "(steady light),",
            "Bottom rows (pulse),",
            "and - if Odd Rows is",
            "on in Settings -",
            "rows 1,3,5,7 (fast",
            "blink), which shows",
            "the whole phrase at",
            "half resolution.",
            "",
            "The third view only",
            "appears on M8s main",
            "SESSION screen. Menu",
            "(Note), Capture",
            "(Sequencer) and",
            "Shift+Back (the",
            "second session",
            "screen) are not",
            "phrase rows, so",
            "every other row",
            "means nothing there",
            "and the cycle drops",
            "back to two stops.",
            "Back returns to",
            "Session, and the",
            "third view with it.",
            "",
            "On the odd view the",
            "Up/Down arrows move",
            "TWO M8 rows a press,",
            "so the next four",
            "even rows come up",
            "instead of the grid",
            "shifting under you.",
            "Shift+Up/Down is not",
            "doubled: a page is",
            "eight rows already,",
            "which is what this",
            "view spans.",
            "",
            "Session: Shift+pad",
            " stops that chain.",
            "",
            "Sequencer, holding a",
            " pad with a note: the",
            " track buttons set",
            " its VELOCITY (four",
            " of the eight levels",
            " at a time - switch",
            " halves for the rest).",
            "",
            "Sequencer, holding a",
            " pad with a phrase:",
            " Up/Down TRANSPOSE",
            " it.",
            "",
            "Colors from M8 are",
            "translated to Move",
            "LED colors in real",
            "time.",
            "",
            "Holding SHIFT makes",
            "knob moves an",
            "AUDITION: turn a",
            "knob while holding",
            "and it goes back to",
            "where it was when",
            "you let go.",
            "",
            "The lit grid is",
            "remembered when you",
            "leave the module and",
            "painted back when you",
            "return, so the pads",
            "come up as you left",
            "them.",
            "",
            "Changing MODE is the",
            "M8's to paint: the",
            "pads go dark and fill",
            "in with what M8 sends",
            "for the new screen,",
            "rather than showing",
            "the old one first.",
            "Switching HALVES",
            "keeps the memory - M8",
            "sends nothing for",
            "that.",
            "",
            "Nothing is asked of",
            "the M8 - on a first",
            "run, with nothing",
            "remembered, the grid",
            "comes up dark until",
            "M8 next paints.",
            "Changing screen on",
            "the M8 does it.",
            "",
            "Play, Rec and the",
            "arrows are painted",
            "only when M8 first",
            "initialises the",
            "surface. To get",
            "them back, toggle",
            "CTRL SURFACE off",
            "and on in M8s MIDI",
            "Settings, or restart",
            "the M8."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Settings",
          "lines": [
            "Shift+Step 2, from",
            "anywhere - the song",
            "list included.",
            "",
            "The pads, transport",
            "and mode buttons",
            "keep working while",
            "this is open. Only",
            "the jogwheel, Back",
            "and Shift gestures",
            "belong to it.",
            "",
            "Jog: move.",
            "Click: edit a row,",
            " click again to",
            " leave it.",
            "Back: up, or close.",
            "",
            "Songs: the song",
            " list.",
            "",
            "Knob Chan: MIDI",
            " channel the 8 song",
            " knobs send on. Must",
            " match M8's CONTROL",
            " MAP CHANNEL (MIDI",
            " Settings view) or",
            " nothing is heard.",
            "",
            "Main Knob: a screen",
            " of its own for knob",
            " 9 - its CC, its MIDI",
            " channel, absolute or",
            " relative send, and",
            " how its value reads",
            " (0-127, Hex, 0-1,",
            " -1..1) in the panel",
            " over the page. Back",
            " returns to Settings.",
            "",
            "Relative is for other",
            " gear - M8 reads",
            " absolute only.",
            "",
            "Knob LED: the colour",
            " sweep the lights",
            " under the knobs walk",
            " as their value",
            " moves. Grey is",
            " black to white;",
            " Syn, Rose and Rain",
            " are colour sweeps;",
            " Off is dark. Knob 9",
            " has no light.",
            "",
            "Odd Rows: adds a",
            " third view to the",
            " mode-button cycle,",
            " on M8s main Session",
            " screen only. See",
            " Pads.",
            "",
            "All of these are",
            "global, not per",
            "song.",
            "",
            "Exit Module: leaves",
            " the module. So does",
            " Shift + volume knob",
            " + jogwheel, the",
            " host's own gesture.",
            " (Shift+Step 13 is",
            " the way INTO the",
            " Tools menu.)",
            "",
            "All of these are also",
            "on the Schwung web",
            "UI, under Modules >",
            "M8 LPP Emulator >",
            "Settings. Changes",
            "made there arrive",
            "within a couple of",
            "seconds; changes",
            "made here show up",
            "there. Last one",
            "wins."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Song Presets",
          "lines": [
            "The 8 step buttons",
            "M8 does not use -",
            "the alternate ones,",
            "between the steps",
            "M8 lights - are",
            "song presets.",
            "",
            "The first 8 songs",
            "sit on them in list",
            "order. Press one to",
            "switch to that",
            "song.",
            "",
            "Amber: the song you",
            " are on.",
            "Ochre: a song is",
            " there.",
            "Dark: nothing on",
            " that button.",
            "",
            "Amber, not white, so",
            "the row cannot be",
            "mistaken for the",
            "track buttons above",
            "it.",
            " that button.",
            "",
            "To change which",
            "button a song is",
            "on, reorder the",
            "list - see Song",
            "Management."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Knobs & Songs",
          "lines": [
            "Display shows the",
            "active song's",
            "knobs as dials with",
            "their names. A",
            "faint tick means an",
            "empty slot.",
            "",
            "Touch or turn a",
            " knob to see its",
            " live value below",
            " the dial, and what",
            " it is connected to",
            " at the top right -",
            " e.g. Ins0A Cut,",
            " Ins0A M2 Amt, REV",
            " Room Size. Let go",
            " and both clear.",
            "",
            "An instrument is",
            " always both of its",
            " hex digits there,",
            " and the words are",
            " abbreviated to fit.",
            "",
            "Knobs 1-8 edit the",
            "shown values and",
            "send their CC to",
            "M8.",
            "",
            "Jog wheel: scroll",
            " through the song's",
            " pages. Pages are",
            " added and removed",
            " automatically as",
            " knobs need them.",
            "",
            "Shift+Step 1: open",
            " Song Management.",
            "Shift+Step 2: open",
            " Settings.",
            "Shift lights the",
            " lamp under step 1",
            " to show it is",
            " there.",
            "",
            "Knob 9 (Main) is a",
            "simple pass-through,",
            "not part of any",
            "song. Turning or",
            "touching it shows",
            "its value in a panel",
            "over the page, and",
            "Shift auditions it",
            "like any other knob.",
            "",
            "Jog Click: a cursor",
            " over the slots. Jog",
            " moves it, and runs",
            " PAST the end onto",
            " the next page. Back",
            " drops it. The pads",
            " and knobs keep",
            " working while it is",
            " up.",
            "",
            "It comes back where",
            " you left it, per",
            " page - wandering to",
            " another page and",
            " back costs neither",
            " its place. A page",
            " not seen yet opens",
            " on its first knob.",
            "",
            "Shift+Jog: move the",
            " knob under the",
            " cursor.",
            "Shift+Copy: dupli-",
            " cate it.",
            "Shift+Delete:",
            " remove it.",
            "Both buttons light",
            " while Shift is",
            " held, if the slot",
            " has a knob.",
            "A graphic moves and",
            " copies whole.",
            "",
            "Jog Click again on",
            " a knob: open Knob",
            " Settings for it -",
            " name, connection,",
            " CC, send mode,",
            " value display, plus",
            " Add and Remove.",
            "",
            "Jog Click on an",
            " EMPTY slot: Add",
            " Knob wizard."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Knob Settings",
          "lines": [
            "Opens from the knob",
            "cursor: Jog Click,",
            "jog to the knob,",
            "Jog Click again.",
            "A list, like Song",
            "Management.",
            "",
            "Jog wheel: move",
            " between Name,",
            " Connect, CC, Mode,",
            " Display.",
            "",
            "Jog Click on Name:",
            " open rename",
            " keyboard.",
            "",
            "Jog Click on CC,",
            " Chan, Mode, Display,",
            " enter/exit editing",
            " that row. While",
            " entered, jog wheel",
            " changes its value:",
            " CC number, channel,",
            " send",
            " mode (Absolute/",
            " Relative), or",
            " display (0-127,",
            " Hex, 0-1, -1..1).",
            "",
            "Hex counts in M8",
            " BYTES, 00-FF, and",
            " sends half of that",
            " - a CC is 7 bits, so",
            " M8 hears every other",
            " one. Every byte is",
            " still reachable.",
            "",
            "Speed: how far one",
            " detent moves it,",
            " in CC steps. 1x is",
            " one CC. 1/2x walks",
            " a hex knob byte by",
            " byte; 1/4x and 1/3x",
            " are finer still; 2x",
            " is twice as fast.",
            "",
            "Min / Max: the ends",
            " of the travel, read",
            " in the knob’s own",
            " display. Shift+jog",
            " moves them by 8.",
            "",
            "ABSOLUTE is the one",
            " M8 understands - it",
            " learns a CC and",
            " reads the value.",
            " Relative sends the",
            " movement instead,",
            " for other gear on",
            " the same wire.",
            " Hex, 0-1, -1..1).",
            "",
            "Connect: what M8",
            " parameter this knob",
            " stands for - shown",
            " at the top right",
            " when you touch it.",
            " A dash means none",
            " is recorded, which",
            " is why the header",
            " cannot name the",
            " instrument. Click",
            " to pick one; the",
            " same lists as Add",
            " Knob.",
            "",
            "It keeps the SLOT",
            " and the CC - the CC",
            " is what M8 has been",
            " taught - and",
            " replaces the name,",
            " the starting value",
            " and the picture. A",
            " knob in a graphic",
            " connects the WHOLE",
            " group.",
            "",
            "Slot: click to",
            " enter, then jog",
            " moves the knob to",
            " another slot,",
            " swapping with",
            " whatever is there.",
            "",
            "A knob that is part",
            " of a graphic moves",
            " the WHOLE group,",
            " keeping it on one",
            " row - so a 4-knob",
            " envelope can only",
            " swap between the",
            " two rows.",
            "",
            " wizard for the",
            " next free slot,",
            " making a new page",
            " if this one is",
            " full.",
            "",
            "Remove Knob: clears",
            " this slot. Others",
            " stay where they",
            " are.",
            "",
            "Touching a",
            " different knob",
            " switches to",
            " editing that one.",
            "",
            "Back: done.",
            "",
            "Chan: which MIDI",
            " channel this knob",
            " sends on. \"Song\"",
            " follows the channel",
            " in Settings; 1-16",
            " pins it to its own,",
            " for a knob aimed at",
            " something that is",
            " not the M8.",
            "",
            "There is no Add Knob",
            "row: adding is Jog",
            "Click on an EMPTY",
            "slot. A full page",
            "has none - turn the",
            "wheel to the spare",
            "page, which is",
            "always there.",
            "",
            "LED: this knob’s own",
            " colour sweep. \"Song\"",
            " follows the one in",
            " Settings."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Add Knob",
          "lines": [
            "Jog Click, jog to",
            "an empty slot, Jog",
            "Click again - or",
            "use Add Knob in",
            "Knob Settings.",
            "",
            "Jog: move.",
            "Click: pick.",
            "Back: up a step,",
            " or out.",
            "",
            "Start by choosing",
            "Generic, Instrument,",
            "Mixer, Sends or EQ.",
            "",
            "GENERIC is one list",
            "of SHAPES, with no",
            "M8 parameter behind",
            "them yet. One click",
            "and the knobs are",
            "there:",
            "",
            " Knob - you type the",
            "  name. For a",
            "  parameter this",
            "  module does not",
            "  know, or for",
            "  something else on",
            "  the same channel.",
            " Envelope (3) and",
            "  Envelope (4).",
            "  M8s AHD, Drum and",
            "  Trig envelopes all",
            "  draw the same",
            "  3-knob picture, so",
            "  they are one row",
            "  here; which one it",
            "  is, is a Connect",
            "  question.",
            " Filter, one row per",
            "  type. ZDF is not",
            "  listed: it draws",
            "  the same curve as",
            "  the plain LP and",
            "  HP, so which of",
            "  the two it is, is",
            "  a Connect question.",
            " LFO, one row per",
            "  wave.",
            "",
            "Use Connect in Knob",
            "Settings afterwards",
            "to say which",
            "instrument and mod",
            "slot it is for. Only",
            "that records the",
            "instrument, so only",
            "then can the header",
            "name it.",
            "",
            "INSTRUMENT asks for",
            "the number first -",
            "the two hex digits",
            "are edited one at a",
            "time, so you never",
            "scroll a list of",
            "128. Then choose:",
            "",
            " Base - amp,",
            "  pan, dry, sends,",
            "  filter.",
            " Mods - pick slot",
            "  1-4, then the mod",
            "  type (AHD, ADSR,",
            "  Drum, LFO, Trig,",
            "  Tracking).",
            " Instrument Type -",
            "  the params only",
            "  that type has.",
            "",
            "New knobs take the",
            "next free CC, start",
            "at M8's default for",
            "that parameter, and",
            "are Hex + Absolute.",
            "",
            "M8 side: map the CC",
            "by putting the",
            "cursor on the",
            "parameter, holding",
            "OPTION and turning",
            "the knob."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Knob Graphics",
          "lines": [
            "Some choices add",
            "SEVERAL knobs that",
            "share one picture",
            "instead of each",
            "drawing its own",
            "dial.",
            "",
            "Filter (3 knobs):",
            " cutoff, resonance",
            " and type, drawn",
            " as the filter's",
            " response curve.",
            "",
            "Envelope (3 or 4):",
            " AHD gives attack,",
            " hold, decay. ADSR",
            " gives attack,",
            " decay, sustain,",
            " release. Drawn as",
            " the envelope",
            " shape.",
            "",
            "LFO (3 knobs):",
            " shape, rate and",
            " depth, drawn as",
            " the wave.",
            "",
            "A picture needs its",
            "knobs side by side",
            "on ONE row, so it",
            "may start a new",
            "row or page.",
            "",
            "Remove knobs until",
            "only one is left",
            "and it goes back to",
            "being a dial.",
            "",
            "LP > HP has two",
            "corners and no",
            "resonance: CUT is the",
            "lowpass (FF = open)",
            "and RES the highpass",
            "(00 = open).",
            "",
            "The knobs are LP then",
            "HP, the same order",
            "the M8 lists them",
            "(CUT above RES), so",
            "learning them down",
            "the M8 screen lands",
            "each on the right",
            "one. Touch a knob and",
            "the header names its",
            "parameter - LP (CUT),",
            "HP (RES) - so you can",
            "check. A crossed pair",
            "looks like the",
            "picture is mirrored.",
            "",
            "LP > HP has no honest",
            "picture (two corners,",
            "no resonance), so it",
            "gets plain dials.",
            "",
            "The Exp Down, Exp Up",
            "and Square Up LFO",
            "shapes need a",
            "Schwung new enough",
            "to draw them. On an",
            "older one they fall",
            "back to dials",
            "automatically."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Song Management",
          "lines": [
            "Shift+Step 1, from",
            "anywhere - Settings",
            "included.",
            "",
            "Back: out.",
            "",
            "First row is",
            "'+ Add Song' -",
            "Jog Click it for a",
            "new song, opens",
            "rename.",
            "",
            "Jog wheel: move",
            " list cursor.",
            "",
            "Shift+Jog wheel:",
            " move the",
            " highlighted song",
            " up or down. This",
            " is how a song is",
            " moved onto a",
            " different preset",
            " step button.",
            "",
            "Jog Click on a",
            " song: switch to",
            " it, close.",
            "",
            "Back: close without",
            " switching.",
            "",
            "Shift+Jog Click:",
            " rename highlighted",
            " song.",
            "",
            "Shift+Copy: dupli-",
            " cate the highligh-",
            " ted song, placed",
            " below it.",
            "",
            "Shift+Delete:",
            " remove it. Asks",
            " first, and starts",
            " on Cancel. The",
            " last song cannot",
            " be deleted.",
            "",
            "Both buttons light",
            " while Shift is",
            " held, on a song",
            " row.",
            "",
            "The song list is also",
            "editable from a",
            "browser: Schwung web",
            "UI, /api/remote-ui/",
            "module-assets/m8/",
            "web_ui.html. Add,",
            "rename, reorder and",
            "delete songs there;",
            "the module picks the",
            "change up within a",
            "couple of seconds,",
            "unless a screen is",
            "open here."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Buttons",
          "lines": [
            "Menu, Back, Capture",
            "and Track buttons",
            "forward to the",
            "Launchpad grid",
            "during normal use.",
            "",
            "See Song Management",
            "for what they do",
            "while that screen",
            "is open.",
            "",
            "Mute and Loop are",
            "the LPP Mute and",
            "Solo. A plain press",
            "switches that",
            "function between",
            "momentary (blinking)",
            "and toggle - it does",
            "not mute anything by",
            "itself.",
            "",
            "The ODD step buttons",
            "(1,3,5..15) are the",
            "LPP's T1-T8 track",
            "buttons: in mute",
            "toggle mode, step 1",
            "mutes track 1. The",
            "even steps between",
            "them are this",
            "module's song",
            "presets."
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}